// Runtime/MailboxRuntime.maxon — the MAILBOX a service receives on, and the four handle/lifetime doors
// around it. The spec is `specs/services.md`: §"Sending MOVES, and that is load-bearing" for
// the ownership rule, §"`ServiceError`" for the poison pill and the last-handle close.
//
// ⭐⭐ **A MAILBOX IS AN INTRUSIVE FIFO OF REQUEST BOXES PLUS TWO REFERENCE COUNTS, AND NOTHING
// ELSE.** The queue is linked through each box's leading `__next` slot
// (`Project.ServiceLinkOffset`). A send appends and returns; a receive pops or PARKS; a close makes
// the queue drainable and un-fillable. What makes it more than a queue is the pair of counts:
// `handles` is how many `<T>.handle` boxes name it (the last one to go CLOSES it, which is the
// whole of "an ordinary program needs no shutdown boilerplate"), and `refs` is that plus the loop
// itself (the last one to go FREES it, which is what lets the loop outlive the handles it is
// draining for).
//
// ⭐⭐ **NO NEW `.data` WORD, AND THAT IS A LAYOUT ARGUMENT AS WELL AS A DESIGN ONE.** Mailbox state
// is per-STRUCT, in the heap, reached from the handle box. A `.data` word would need a
// `MultiMSharing` class (`SchedRuntime.pushRuntimeGlobal` PANICS without one) and would shift every
// label after it, moving **every heap program's `data {` table** — `SlabRuntime`'s own header
// records that cost for the allocator's lock, which lives in its state region for exactly this
// reason.
//
// ⛔⛔ **HARD RULE, AND IT IS WHY THE RECEIVE PARK IS DEFERRED: NO MAILBOX LOCK IS EVER HELD ACROSS
// `__gt_context_switch`.** Every host lock is recursive on the WRONG IDENTITY — a Win32
// CRITICAL_SECTION is per-OS-THREAD while green threads multiplex over one — so a GT that parked while
// holding one would let another GT on the same M take the recursive path straight into the critical section.
// That is not a deadlock; it is silent FIFO corruption, which is worse. `__mbox_recv` therefore RELEASES
// before it parks and re-checks after it wakes, and the registration that makes it discoverable happens in
// `__gt_register_park`'s mailbox arm, on the machine's scheduler context, after the switch has saved its
// registers.

// head, tail, parkedGt and closed are read and written only under the mailbox lock, because
// `__mbox_recv`'s decision to park rests on "empty, open and nobody parked" being one instant
// across three words. The two counts are `lock xadd` instead: each is one word whose transaction
// is exactly its own increment.
let MboxOffHead = 0x00
let MboxOffTail = 0x08

// ⚠ **NAMED `parkedGt` AND NOT `waiter`, BECAUSE `GtOffWaiter` IS A DIFFERENT FACT ABOUT THE SAME THREAD.**
// A GT's `waiter` is the scheduler context that switched it in — who to context-switch back to.
// This is the green thread parked in `__mbox_recv` on THIS mailbox, i.e. who to make `ready` when a
// request arrives. Two fields called `waiter` in one wake sequence is exactly the confusion that
// writes a status into the wrong struct.
let MboxOffParkedGt = 0x10

// Non-zero once the mailbox has been closed — by the last handle drop, or by the loop on its way out after a
// `__shutdown` pill. A send to a closed mailbox ABANDONS its request rather than queueing it, and a receive
// on a closed EMPTY one answers 0, which is how the loop learns to exit.
let MboxOffClosed = 0x18

let MboxOffHandles = 0x20
let MboxOffRefs = 0x28

// The request union's DROP CASCADE, as an address. It is what makes a closed mailbox's queue
// droppable at all: only the cascade knows the payload types of a queued `<T>.request` box's live
// variant. A closure-based mailbox could not know what to free, which is why the request is a
// synthesized union.
let MboxOffAbandonFn = 0x30

// ⭐⭐ **THE `__shutdown` PILL'S REPLY CELL, PARKED HERE UNTIL THE SERVICE HAS FINISHED, OR 0.** It is
// what makes `await h.shutdown()` a real DRAINED rendezvous rather than a "the pill was dequeued" one: the
// loop's pill arm stores the cell here and `__mbox_service_exit` — the loop's last act, after the queue is
// drained and the state is dropped — answers it. `ServiceLoop.buildShutdownPillArm` states why it is a mailbox
// word rather than a value threaded through the drain loop as a block argument.
//
// ⚠ **IT IS WRITTEN AND READ BY THE SERVICE'S OWN GREEN THREAD ONLY**, which is why it is a plain store
// where the four words above it are the mailbox lock's: nothing else in the process can reach a mailbox's
// shutdown cell, because nothing else runs `<T>.__loop`.
//
// ⚠ EXPORTED, unlike its six siblings, because the site that WRITES it is the Maxon-tier `<T>.__loop`
// (`ServiceLoop`) while the site that reads it is `__mbox_service_exit` here — the two files must spell one
// number, which is `GtParkKind`'s rule read from the other end.
export let MboxOffShutdownReply = 0x38 as ByteOffset

// The lock order is `__sched_lock` → mailbox lock: `__gt_register_park`'s mailbox arm takes this
// lock inside its `__sched_lock` hold. Nothing that takes another lock runs while it is held — the
// wake readies after the release, and the closed road releases before the drop cascade — so a path
// that took `__sched_lock` under it would deadlock against that arm.
let MboxOffLock = 0x40 as ByteOffset
let MboxRegionBytes = (MboxOffLock as FullRangeInt) + OsLockBytes

// The two counts' initial values, named because they are a PAIR and their difference is the whole lifetime
// rule: one handle names the mailbox, and the loop is the second thing that keeps it alive.
let MboxInitialHandles = 1
let MboxInitialRefs = 2

// A count step, as the `lock xadd` operand. `xadd` answers the PRIOR value, so "I was the last" is
// `prior == 1` — read off the displaced value rather than from a re-read, which is the same discipline
// `MmRuntime.emitRefcountCheckToLastOwner` states for a decref.
let MboxCountUp = 1
let MboxCountDown = -1
let MboxLastOwner = 1

// The value stored into `closed`. Any non-zero would do; the constant is what stops a reader spelling `1`
// and a writer spelling something else.
let MboxIsClosed = 1

// --- Entry points ---

// ⭐⭐ **`__svc_spawn(loopPtr, state, abandonPtr) -> mbox` — CREATE THE MAILBOX AND THE GREEN THREAD THAT
// SERVES IT, IN THAT ORDER.** The mailbox exists before the thread does, because the thread's second
// argument IS the mailbox; and the thread is published LAST, once both its argument slots are written, for
// `GtRuntime.GtReadyName`'s measured reason (a worker M dequeues and runs a spawned thread while the
// spawning thread is still storing its arguments).
//
// ⚠ **IT ANSWERS THE MAILBOX AND NOT A HANDLE BOX.** The `<T>.handle` box is allocated by the PARSER, at
// `emitBoxAlloc` — the one `__mm_alloc` door, which is where the box header's destructor argument is decided
// — and this pointer is stored into its one field. A runtime-minted box would be a second place that knows
// what a managed record costs.
export let SvcSpawnName = b"__svc_spawn"

// `__mbox_send(mbox, box)` — append one request, or abandon it if the mailbox is already closed. It
// completes INLINE and never suspends, which is why it is deliberately NOT on `SemanticCheck`'s park roster:
// listing it would let `async` wrap a genuinely non-yielding function.
export let MboxSendName = b"__mbox_send"

// ⭐ `__mbox_recv(mbox) -> box | 0` — the loop's only blocking operation, and the one mailbox entry that IS
// a park point. It answers 0 exactly once: when the mailbox is closed AND drained.
export let MboxRecvName = b"__mbox_recv"

// EXPORTED because the LOOP closes its own mailbox on the way out — a `__shutdown` pill stops the service
// while its handles are still alive, and the close is what makes what is queued behind it drainable.
export let MboxCloseName = b"__mbox_close"

// `__mbox_handle_clone_box(handleBox) -> handleBox` — a second HANDLE to the SAME service, never a second
// service. Exported because `SignatureIndex.managedNameCascadeStrategy` routes `<T>.handle`'s clone here.
export let MboxHandleCloneBoxName = b"__mbox_handle_clone_box"

// `__mbox_handle_drop_box(handleBox)` — one handle goes; the LAST one closes the mailbox. Exported because
// `SignatureIndex.managedNameDropCallee` routes `<T>.handle`'s drop here, which is what makes an ordinary
// scope exit, an array element drop and a struct-field cascade all shut a service down.
export let MboxHandleDropBoxName = b"__mbox_handle_drop_box"

// ⭐⭐⭐ **`__mbox_handle_retain_box(handleBox)` — THE EXACT MIRROR OF THE DROP.** A `<T>.handle`
// value owns THREE things — a share of the mailbox's `handles` count, a share of its `refs` count,
// and a reference to the little box that names it — and `__mbox_handle_drop_box` releases all
// three, so a retain acquires all three. A bare `__mm_incref` of the box, which a generic co-own
// path emits for an ordinary managed record, acquires only the third.
//
// ⇒ **TWO OWNERS, ONE SHARE, TWO RELEASES.** Under a bare incref, `let w = spawn T.create()` then
// `arr.push(w)` increfs the box to 2, and each of the two eventual drops steps `handles` and `refs`
// DOWN — so the mailbox is closed and **FREED while the array's handle still names it**, and the
// second drop frees it again: exit 89 (`RuntimeAbort.slabFreeOfParkedSpan`), 101 or a segfault,
// depending on the processor count. `arr.push(spawn T.create())` cannot show it, because a
// temporary's one reference is MOVED and never increfed.
//
// ⚠ **SO THE INVARIANT IS: EVERY REFERENCE TO A HANDLE BOX OWNS ONE SHARE OF EACH COUNT.** A clone takes a
// FRESH box and one share of each (`__mbox_handle_clone_box`); a retain takes a SECOND REFERENCE to an
// existing box and one share of each; a drop gives back one of each. All three step the pair, and the pair
// is what decides when the service stops and when its record is freed.
export let MboxHandleRetainBoxName = b"__mbox_handle_retain_box"

// `__mbox_service_exit(mbox)` — the loop's last act. Exported because `ServiceLoop` emits the call as the
// tail of every synthesized `<T>.__loop`.
export let MboxServiceExitName = b"__mbox_service_exit"

// ⭐⭐ **`__mbox_abandon(mbox, box)` — GIVE ONE UNDELIVERED REQUEST TO THIS MAILBOX'S OWN ABANDON
// FUNCTION.** Both roads to an abandoned message reach `<T>.__abandon`, and they reach it from
// opposite tiers: `__mbox_send`'s closed arm has the mailbox in a register, and the loop's DRAIN is
// Maxon-tier code that cannot NAME the symbol — `<T>.__abandon` is synthesized, so a call to it by
// name is `E3004: call to undefined function` from the very pass that walks the synthesized body.
// Asking the mailbox is what both can do, and it also means the drain and the send cannot come to
// abandon through two different functions.
export let MboxAbandonName = b"__mbox_abandon"

// ⭐⭐ **INSTALL THE MAILBOX RUNTIME — behind `usesGt`, at its CALL SITE, exactly as `installSchedRuntime`
// is.** There is no program that wants a mailbox without the green-thread substrate under it: `__svc_spawn`
// calls `__gt_spawn_green` and every wake goes through `__gt_ready_locked`. And there is no bit of its
// own to gate it with, for `SlabRuntime.SlabScavengeName`'s stated reason — these functions gate nothing
// (no import, no `.data` slot, no per-allocation maintenance), and `DeadFunctionElimination` drops them all
// from every program that never spawns a service, because the only edge into them is the `funcAddr`/`call`
// pair `LowerMaxonToStd.lowerServiceSpawn` emits.

export function installMailboxRuntime(module StdModule)
	buildSvcSpawn(module)
	buildMboxSend(module)
	buildMboxRecv(module)
	buildMboxClose(module)
	buildMboxHandleCloneBox(module)
	buildMboxHandleRetainBox(module)
	buildMboxHandleDropBox(module)
	buildMboxServiceExit(module)
	buildMboxAbandon(module)
	buildMboxInterfaceCloneBox(module)
	buildMboxInterfaceSend(module)
end 'installMailboxRuntime'

let MboxInterfaceRuntimePrefix = b"__mbox_iface_"
export let MboxInterfaceCloneBoxName = b"__mbox_iface_clone_box"
export let MboxInterfaceSendName = b"__mbox_iface_send"
let MboxInterfaceConversionPrefix = b"__mbox_iface_from."
let MboxInterfaceStubPrefix = b"__mbox_iface_stub."
let MboxInterfaceTablePrefix = b"__mbox_iface_table."
let MboxInterfaceSlotBytes = 8

export function isInterfaceHandleRuntimeCallee(callee ByteArray) returns bool
	return bytesStartWith(callee, prefix: MboxInterfaceRuntimePrefix)
end 'isInterfaceHandleRuntimeCallee'

export function isInterfaceHandleConversionCallee(callee ByteArray) returns bool
	return bytesStartWith(callee, prefix: MboxInterfaceConversionPrefix)
end 'isInterfaceHandleConversionCallee'

export function interfaceHandleConversionName(serviceTypeName ByteArray, interfaceName ByteArray) returns ByteArray
	return "{String.from(MboxInterfaceConversionPrefix)}{String.from(serviceTypeName)}.{String.from(interfaceName)}".toByteArray()
end 'interfaceHandleConversionName'

function interfaceHandleStubName(serviceTypeName ByteArray, interfaceName ByteArray, slot CaseIndex) returns ByteArray
	return "{String.from(MboxInterfaceStubPrefix)}{String.from(serviceTypeName)}.{String.from(interfaceName)}.{slot}".toByteArray()
end 'interfaceHandleStubName'

function interfaceHandleTableLabel(serviceTypeName ByteArray, interfaceName ByteArray) returns String
	return "{String.from(MboxInterfaceTablePrefix)}{String.from(serviceTypeName)}.{String.from(interfaceName)}"
end 'interfaceHandleTableLabel'

export function interfaceSendSlotOffset(slot CaseIndex) returns FullRangeInt
	return (slot as FullRangeInt) * MboxInterfaceSlotBytes
end 'interfaceSendSlotOffset'

function buildMboxInterfaceCloneBox(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxInterfaceCloneBoxName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let handleBox = 0

	let mbox = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: handleBox, offset: ServiceHandleMailboxOffset, ids: ids)
	let table = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: handleBox, offset: InterfaceHandleTableOffset, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.ret(emitInterfaceHandleBox(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, table: table, ids: ids)))
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxInterfaceCloneBox'

function emitInterfaceHandleBox(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, table ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	emitMailboxShareTaken(module, block: block, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	return emitInterfaceHandleBoxHolding(module, block: block, mbox: mbox, table: table, ids: ids)
end 'emitInterfaceHandleBox'

module function emitMailboxShareTaken(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, ids ValueMinter)
	_ = emitMboxCountStep(module, block: block, mbox: mbox, offset: MboxOffHandles, delta: MboxCountUp, ids: ids)
	_ = emitMboxCountStep(module, block: block, mbox: mbox, offset: MboxOffRefs, delta: MboxCountUp, ids: ids)
end 'emitMailboxShareTaken'

module function emitInterfaceHandleBoxHolding(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, table ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	let boxBytes = emitConst(module, block: block, value: InterfaceHandleBoxSize, ids: ids)
	let trivial = emitConst(module, block: block, value: TrivialDestructor, ids: ids)
	let box = ids.mint()
	emitMmAllocCall(module, block: block, result: box, size: boxBytes, destructor: trivial, tag: mmTagIndex(MmTag.Untagged), ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: block, record: box, offset: ServiceHandleMailboxOffset, value: mbox)
	emitStoreField(module, block: block, record: box, offset: InterfaceHandleTableOffset, value: table)
	return box
end 'emitInterfaceHandleBoxHolding'

function buildMboxInterfaceSend(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxInterfaceSendName, returnType: StdReturnType.void, paramCount: 3, paramTypes: threeI64Params())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(3)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 3)
	let handleBox = 0
	let slotOffset = 1
	let request = 2

	let mbox = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: handleBox, offset: ServiceHandleMailboxOffset, ids: ids)
	let table = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: handleBox, offset: InterfaceHandleTableOffset, ids: ids)
	let stub = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: emitBin(module, block: entry, a: table, b: slotOffset, opcode: StdBinOpcode.add, ids: ids), offset: 0, ids: ids)
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.callIndirect(ids.mint(), calleeReg: stub, resultType: StdReturnType.void, argFloatMask: 0, args: twoArgs(mbox, second: request)))
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.retVoid)
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxInterfaceSend'

// Every interface with a handle, not only the service's own `conformsTo`: a handle widens to an interface
// its service reaches through `extends` (`ProgramSignatures.serviceHandleWidensTo`), and that conversion is
// called too.
export function installInterfaceHandleConversions(module StdModule, globalData GlobalDataTable, usage RuntimeUsage, signatures ProgramSignatures)
	if usage.neededInterfaceConversions.count() == 0 'noConversion'
		return
	end 'noConversion'

	var built = 0 as Count

	for serviceTypeName in serviceCompanionRoster(signatures) 'eachService'
		for interfaceName in signatures.interfacesWithHandles() 'eachInterfaceHandle'
			if usage.neededInterfaceConversions.contains(interfaceHandleConversionName(serviceTypeName, interfaceName: interfaceName)) 'thisPairIsConverted'
				buildInterfaceHandleConversion(module, globalData: globalData, signatures: signatures, serviceTypeName: serviceTypeName, interfaceName: interfaceName)
				built = built + 1
			end 'thisPairIsConverted'
		end 'eachInterfaceHandle'
	end 'eachService'

	if built != usage.neededInterfaceConversions.count() 'aConversionOfADeadService'
		panic("installInterfaceHandleConversions: {usage.neededInterfaceConversions.count()} conversion(s) are called and {built} were built — a reached body converts the handle of a service that is not on the companion roster, the set `ServiceCompanions.interfaceServiceImplementers` vets")
	end 'aConversionOfADeadService'
end 'installInterfaceHandleConversions'

function buildInterfaceHandleConversion(module StdModule, globalData GlobalDataTable, signatures ProgramSignatures, serviceTypeName ByteArray, interfaceName ByteArray)
	let interfaceRequest = requireServiceRequestLayout(signatures, typeName: interfaceName)
	let serviceRequest = requireServiceRequestLayout(signatures, typeName: serviceTypeName)
	let label = interfaceHandleTableLabel(serviceTypeName, interfaceName: interfaceName)
	var blob = ByteArray.create()
	blob.growFilled(interfaceSendSlotOffset(interfaceRequest.caseCount()) as ElementIndex, value: 0)
	_ = globalData.registerRdataConstantLabeled(label, bytes: blob, kind: RdataPayloadKind.witnessTable)

	for slot in 0 upto interfaceRequest.caseCount() 'eachSlot'
		let serviceCase = try serviceRequest.indexOfCase(interfaceRequest.caseNameAt(slot)) otherwise panic("buildInterfaceHandleConversion: `{String.from(serviceTypeName)}` has no message `{String.from(interfaceRequest.caseNameAt(slot))}` of `{String.from(interfaceName)}` — conformance requires every requirement, and a message is an exported instance method")

		let stubName = interfaceHandleStubName(serviceTypeName, interfaceName: interfaceName, slot: slot)
		buildInterfaceSendStub(module, name: stubName, serviceTag: serviceRequest.tagOfIndex(serviceCase))
		globalData.recordFuncAbs64InRdata(stubName, rdataLabel: label, offsetInLabel: interfaceSendSlotOffset(slot) as ByteOffset)
	end 'eachSlot'

	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(interfaceHandleConversionName(serviceTypeName, interfaceName: interfaceName), returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)
	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let serviceHandle = 0

	let mbox = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: serviceHandle, offset: ServiceHandleMailboxOffset, ids: ids)
	let table = ids.mint()
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.rdataAddr(table, label: globalData.labelBytesOf(label)))
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.ret(emitInterfaceHandleBox(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, table: table, ids: ids)))
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildInterfaceHandleConversion'

function buildInterfaceSendStub(module StdModule, name ByteArray, serviceTag FullRangeInt)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(name, returnType: StdReturnType.void, paramCount: 2, paramTypes: twoI64Params())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(2)
	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 2)
	let mbox = 0
	let request = 1

	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: request, offset: UnionTagOffset, value: emitConst(module, block: entry, value: serviceTag, ids: ids))
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.call(ids.mint(), callee: MboxSendName, args: twoArgs(mbox, second: request)))
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.retVoid)
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildInterfaceSendStub'

function emitMboxLockEnter(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, ids ValueMinter)
	emitSchedStepLockDepth(module, block: block, delta: OneMore, ids: ids)
	module.appendOp(block, op: StdOp.osLockEnter(emitFieldAddr(module, block: block, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffLock, ids: ids)))
end 'emitMboxLockEnter'

function emitMboxLockLeave(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, ids ValueMinter)
	module.appendOp(block, op: StdOp.osLockLeave(emitFieldAddr(module, block: block, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffLock, ids: ids)))
	emitSchedStepLockDepth(module, block: block, delta: OneFewer, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxLockLeave'

function emitMboxFree(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, ids ValueMinter)
	module.appendOp(block, op: StdOp.osLockDestroy(emitFieldAddr(module, block: block, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffLock, ids: ids)))
	emitSlabFree(module, block: block, ptr: mbox, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxFree'

// The wake an arriving request and a close both owe. The caller holds the mailbox lock on entry
// and nothing on return. `parkedGt` is taken and cleared under the lock the receiver re-checks and
// publishes under, so a receiver either is found here or sees the event on its re-check, and a
// second waker finds nobody to ready twice.
function emitMboxWakeAndUnlock(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, mbox ValueId, ids ValueMinter, label ByteArray) returns IrBlock
	var wakeParked = module.addBlock(func, label: label, heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	let cont = module.addBlock(func, label: b"mboxwoken", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	let parked = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffParkedGt, ids: ids)
	let noneParked = emitConst(module, block: cur, value: 0, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffParkedGt, value: noneParked)
	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: cur, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	let nobodyWaiting = emitCompareWithConstant(module, block: cur, value: parked, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: 0, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(cur, op: StdOp.condBranch(nobodyWaiting, thenBlockId: cont.id, elseBlockId: wakeParked.id))

	emitGtReadyParkedService(module, func: func, cur: wakeParked, service: parked, cont: cont, ids: ids)
	return cont
end 'emitMboxWakeAndUnlock'

// One count stepped by `delta`, answering whether the caller was the LAST owner — `prior == 1` on a step
// down. Both counts are read this way and neither is ever re-read, which is what makes "was I the last?"
// a property of the instruction rather than of two loads with a window between them.
function emitMboxCountStep(module StdModule, block IrBlock, mbox ValueId, offset ByteOffset, delta FullRangeInt, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	let addr = emitFieldAddr(module, block: block, record: mbox, offset: offset, ids: ids)
	let step = emitConst(module, block: block, value: delta, ids: ids)
	let prior = ids.mint()
	module.appendOp(block, op: StdOp.atomicRmw(prior, addrId: addr, operandId: step, opcode: StdAtomicRmwOpcode.add))
	return prior
end 'emitMboxCountStep'

// Was the step this caller just made the last one — i.e. did the count go 1 -> 0?
function emitMboxWasLastOwner(module StdModule, block IrBlock, prior ValueId, ids ValueMinter) returns ValueId
	return emitCompareWithConstant(module, block: block, value: prior, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: MboxLastOwner, ids: ids)
end 'emitMboxWasLastOwner'

// `__svc_spawn(loopPtr, state, abandonPtr) -> mbox`. See `SvcSpawnName`.
function buildSvcSpawn(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(SvcSpawnName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 3, paramTypes: threeI64Params())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(3)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 3)
	let loopPtr = 0
	let state = 1
	let abandonPtr = 2

	// `__slab_alloc` ZEROES, so head/tail/parkedGt/closed are already their correct initial state and only
	// the three words a zero would be wrong for are stored.
	let mboxBytes = emitConst(module, block: entry, value: MboxRegionBytes, ids: ids)
	let mbox = ids.mint()
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.call(mbox, callee: SlabAllocName, args: argsOf(mboxBytes)))
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.osLockInit(emitFieldAddr(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffLock, ids: ids)))
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffHandles, value: emitConst(module, block: entry, value: MboxInitialHandles, ids: ids))
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffRefs, value: emitConst(module, block: entry, value: MboxInitialRefs, ids: ids))
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffAbandonFn, value: abandonPtr)

	// ⭐⭐ **`__gt_spawn_green`, NOT `__gt_spawn` — a SERVICE IS A GREEN THREAD AND NOT A COROUTINE.** The two
	// bodies differ in one store (a coroutine copies its spawner's owner; a green thread is stamped with
	// itself), and that store is what makes this thread the head of a strand of its own, whose token goes to a
	// P's RING, rather than a member of its spawner's strand. A coroutine here would run only where its
	// spawner's work runs, which is exactly the property a service must not have.
	let gt = ids.mint()
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.call(gt, callee: GtSpawnGreenName, args: argsOf(loopPtr)))
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: gt, offset: GtOffArgInline as ByteOffset, value: state)
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: gt, offset: (GtOffArgInline + GtArgSlotBytes) as ByteOffset, value: mbox)
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.call(ids.mint(), callee: GtReadyName, args: argsOf(gt)))

	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.ret(mbox))
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildSvcSpawn'

// `__mbox_send(mbox, box)`. See `MboxSendName`.
function buildMboxSend(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxSendName, returnType: StdReturnType.void, paramCount: 2, paramTypes: twoI64Params())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(2)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var abandon = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendclosed", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var append = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendappend", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var firstRequest = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendfirst", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var chainRequest = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendchain", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var linked = module.addBlock(func, label: b"sendlinked", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var doneBlock = module.addBlock(func, label: b"senddone", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 2)
	let mbox = 0
	let box = 1

	emitMboxLockEnter(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	let closed = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffClosed, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: entry, value: closed, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: 0, whenTrue: append, whenFalse: abandon, ids: ids)

	// ⭐⭐ **THE CLOSED ARM IS REACHABLE AND IS NOT A RACE-ONLY SAFETY NET.** The LOOP closes the mailbox on
	// its way out after a `__shutdown` pill, and the handles are still alive at that moment — so an author
	// who writes `h.shutdown()` and then sends again arrives here. The request is dropped through the union's
	// own cascade, which is the same drop the exit drain performs on whatever was already queued; whichever
	// of the two roads a given send takes is a race, and BOTH must leak nothing
	// (`specs/services.md:a-send-after-shutdown-is-dropped-cleanly` is that measurement).
	//
	// ⚠ **THE LOCK IS RELEASED FIRST, BECAUSE THE CASCADE IS USER-SHAPED CODE.** `__destruct_<T>.request`
	// frees whatever the live variant owns — a String, a nested box, another service's handle — and a handle
	// drop reaches `__mbox_close`, which takes this very lock. A recursive re-entry would be safe and its
	// LEAVE would release nothing, which is the silent hang `GtRuntime.GtRunnerDoneName` records for the
	// neighbouring rule.
	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: abandon, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.appendOp(abandon, op: StdOp.call(ids.mint(), callee: MboxAbandonName, args: twoArgs(mbox, second: box)))
	module.setTerminator(abandon, op: StdOp.branch(doneBlock.id))

	let emptyQueue = emitConst(module, block: append, value: 0, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: append, record: box, offset: ServiceLinkOffset, value: emptyQueue)
	let tail = emitLoadField(module, block: append, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffTail, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: append, value: tail, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: 0, whenTrue: firstRequest, whenFalse: chainRequest, ids: ids)

	emitStoreField(module, block: firstRequest, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffHead, value: box)
	module.setTerminator(firstRequest, op: StdOp.branch(linked.id))

	emitStoreField(module, block: chainRequest, record: tail, offset: ServiceLinkOffset, value: box)
	module.setTerminator(chainRequest, op: StdOp.branch(linked.id))

	emitStoreField(module, block: linked, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffTail, value: box)
	var woken = emitMboxWakeAndUnlock(module, func: func, cur: linked, mbox: mbox, ids: ids, label: b"sendwakeparked")
	module.setTerminator(woken, op: StdOp.branch(doneBlock.id))

	module.setTerminator(doneBlock, op: StdOp.retVoid)
	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxSend'

// `__mbox_recv(mbox) -> box | 0`. See `MboxRecvName`.
function buildMboxRecv(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxRecvName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var attempt = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvtry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var pop = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvpop", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var clearTail = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvlast", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var popped = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvpopped", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var emptyQueue = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvempty", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var drained = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvdrained", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var park = module.addBlock(func, label: b"recvpark", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let mbox = 0
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.branch(attempt.id))

	emitMboxLockEnter(module, block: attempt, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	let head = emitLoadField(module, block: attempt, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffHead, ids: ids)
	let noRequest = emitConst(module, block: attempt, value: 0, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: attempt, value: head, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: 0, whenTrue: emptyQueue, whenFalse: pop, ids: ids)

	let next = emitLoadField(module, block: pop, record: head, offset: ServiceLinkOffset, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: pop, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffHead, value: next)
	let lastRequest = emitCmp(module, block: pop, a: next, b: noRequest, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(pop, op: StdOp.condBranch(lastRequest, thenBlockId: clearTail.id, elseBlockId: popped.id))

	emitStoreField(module, block: clearTail, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffTail, value: noRequest)
	module.setTerminator(clearTail, op: StdOp.branch(popped.id))

	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: popped, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(popped, op: StdOp.ret(head))

	// ⭐ **THE `closed` READ IS INSIDE THE SAME CRITICAL SECTION THE HEAD READ WAS**, which is what makes
	// "empty AND closed" one instant rather than two: a close that landed between two separate reads would
	// leave this thread parking on a mailbox nobody will ever send to again.
	let closed = emitLoadField(module, block: emptyQueue, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffClosed, ids: ids)
	let stillOpen = emitCmp(module, block: emptyQueue, a: closed, b: noRequest, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, ids: ids)
	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: emptyQueue, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(emptyQueue, op: StdOp.condBranch(stillOpen, thenBlockId: park.id, elseBlockId: drained.id))

	module.setTerminator(drained, op: StdOp.ret(noRequest))

	// ⭐⭐ **THE REGISTRATION IS `__gt_register_park`'s AND THE LOCK IS ALREADY RELEASED — the two halves of this
	// file's hard rule.** `emitGtPark` leaves a NOTE on the green thread and switches to its machine's
	// scheduler context, and `__gt_register_park`'s mailbox arm then performs the registration, re-checking head
	// and `closed` under the lock and UNDOING the park if either has changed. Between this release and that
	// registration a sender can arrive, find `parkedGt` still 0 and wake nobody — and the re-check is what
	// notices. Resuming re-enters `attempt`, which takes the lock and asks again, so a spurious wake costs a
	// loop iteration and nothing else.
	emitGtPark(module, ids: ids, cur: park, kind: GtParkKind.mailbox.rawValue, arg: mbox, cont: attempt)

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxRecv'

// `__mbox_close(mbox)` — make the queue un-fillable and drainable, and wake whoever is parked on it so the
// loop can observe that. Idempotent: both roads to it (the last handle drop, and the loop's own exit after a
// `__shutdown` pill) may run, in either order.
function buildMboxClose(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxCloseName, returnType: StdReturnType.void, paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let mbox = 0

	emitMboxLockEnter(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffClosed, value: emitConst(module, block: entry, value: MboxIsClosed, ids: ids))
	var woken = emitMboxWakeAndUnlock(module, func: func, cur: entry, mbox: mbox, ids: ids, label: b"closewakeparked")
	module.setTerminator(woken, op: StdOp.retVoid)

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxClose'

// `__mbox_handle_clone_box(handleBox) -> handleBox`. See `MboxHandleCloneBoxName`.
//
// ⚠ **BOTH COUNTS GO UP, AND THE SECOND IS NOT REDUNDANT.** `handles` decides when the mailbox CLOSES and
// `refs` when it is FREED; a clone adds a namer of the mailbox and therefore one of each. Stepping only
// `handles` would let the drop of the original free a record its clone still points at.
function buildMboxHandleCloneBox(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxHandleCloneBoxName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let handleBox = 0

	let mbox = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: handleBox, offset: ServiceHandleMailboxOffset, ids: ids)
	_ = emitMboxCountStep(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, offset: MboxOffHandles, delta: MboxCountUp, ids: ids)
	_ = emitMboxCountStep(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, offset: MboxOffRefs, delta: MboxCountUp, ids: ids)

	// A FRESH box, on the same `__mm_alloc` contract every handle box is born through — a clone that answered
	// the same box would make the drop of either free a record the other still names.
	//
	// ⛔⛔ **THROUGH `emitMmAllocCall`, BECAUSE `__mm_alloc`'s ARITY IS `--debugstream`'s.** A hand-written
	// two-argument call here is a call one argument short of the callee a traced build defines, which is what
	// that function's header predicts of any site that spells the call itself.
	//
	// ⭐ The tag is `Untagged` because THIS body has no type to name: one Std-tier entry serves every service,
	// and the handle's companion struct is not reachable from it — the same answer, for the same reason, as
	// `__mm_retain`'s box copy.
	let boxBytes = emitConst(module, block: entry, value: ServiceHandleBoxSize, ids: ids)
	let trivial = emitConst(module, block: entry, value: TrivialDestructor, ids: ids)
	let cloned = ids.mint()
	emitMmAllocCall(module, block: entry, result: cloned, size: boxBytes, destructor: trivial, tag: mmTagIndex(MmTag.Untagged), ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: entry, record: cloned, offset: ServiceHandleMailboxOffset, value: mbox)
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.ret(cloned))

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxHandleCloneBox'

// `__mbox_handle_retain_box(handleBox) -> handleBox`. See `MboxHandleRetainBoxName` for the double free its
// absence was.
//
// ⚠ **IT IS THE DROP READ BACKWARDS, INCLUDING THE ORDER.** The drop is close-then-release because
// `__mbox_close` reads the record and needs `refs` to still be holding it; going up there is no such
// hazard — nothing is freed on this road — so the two steps are simply both taken before the box's own
// incref. What matters is that the SET is the same set: miss either count here and the drop's matching step
// runs one time too many, which is the failure this function exists to prevent.
//
// ⭐ **IT HANDS THE BOX BACK, WHICH IS WHAT LETS ONE ENTRY SERVE BOTH RETAIN SHAPES.** The plain-box family
// needs two entries — `__mm_incref` where the caller already holds the ValueId, `__mm_retain` where a FRESH
// SSA name for the same box is what it needs — and a second handle entry would be the `handles`/`refs` pair
// written down twice. A caller that wants no name ignores the result, exactly as it ignores `__mm_alloc`'s
// when it is emitting for effect.
function buildMboxHandleRetainBox(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxHandleRetainBoxName, returnType: StdReturnType.value(StdType.i64), paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let handleBox = 0 as ValueId

	let mbox = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: handleBox, offset: ServiceHandleMailboxOffset, ids: ids)
	_ = emitMboxCountStep(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, offset: MboxOffHandles, delta: MboxCountUp, ids: ids)
	_ = emitMboxCountStep(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, offset: MboxOffRefs, delta: MboxCountUp, ids: ids)
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.call(ids.mint(), callee: MmIncrefName, args: argsOf(handleBox)))
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.ret(handleBox))

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxHandleRetainBox'

// `__mbox_handle_drop_box(handleBox)`. See `MboxHandleDropBoxName`.
//
// ⭐⭐ **THE ORDER IS CLOSE-THEN-RELEASE, AND REVERSING IT IS A USE-AFTER-FREE.** `__mbox_close` reads and
// writes the record, so the reference this frame holds has to outlive it — which is exactly what `refs`
// counts. So: step `handles` and close if this was the last namer; only THEN step `refs` and free if this
// was the last owner.
function buildMboxHandleDropBox(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxHandleDropBoxName, returnType: StdReturnType.void, paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var closeIt = module.addBlock(func, label: b"dropclose", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var releaseRef = module.addBlock(func, label: b"droprelease", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var freeMbox = module.addBlock(func, label: b"dropfree", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var doneBlock = module.addBlock(func, label: b"dropdone", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let handleBox = 0

	let mbox = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: handleBox, offset: ServiceHandleMailboxOffset, ids: ids)
	let priorHandles = emitMboxCountStep(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, offset: MboxOffHandles, delta: MboxCountDown, ids: ids)
	let wasLastHandle = emitMboxWasLastOwner(module, block: entry, prior: priorHandles, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.condBranch(wasLastHandle, thenBlockId: closeIt.id, elseBlockId: releaseRef.id))

	module.appendOp(closeIt, op: StdOp.call(ids.mint(), callee: MboxCloseName, args: argsOf(mbox)))
	module.setTerminator(closeIt, op: StdOp.branch(releaseRef.id))

	let priorRefs = emitMboxCountStep(module, block: releaseRef, mbox: mbox, offset: MboxOffRefs, delta: MboxCountDown, ids: ids)
	let wasLastRef = emitMboxWasLastOwner(module, block: releaseRef, prior: priorRefs, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(releaseRef, op: StdOp.condBranch(wasLastRef, thenBlockId: freeMbox.id, elseBlockId: doneBlock.id))

	emitMboxFree(module, block: freeMbox, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(freeMbox, op: StdOp.branch(doneBlock.id))

	// The handle BOX itself is an ordinary managed record with a trivial destructor, so it goes back through
	// the ordinary decref — the mailbox above is what this entry exists to say something extra about.
	module.appendOp(doneBlock, op: StdOp.call(ids.mint(), callee: MmDecrefName, args: argsOf(handleBox)))
	module.setTerminator(doneBlock, op: StdOp.retVoid)

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxHandleDropBox'

// `__mbox_service_exit(mbox)` — the loop's last act. See `MboxServiceExitName`.
//
// ⚠⚠ **THE CONSUMER TICKET IS ADDED FROM INSIDE THE GREEN THREAD, AND ADDING IT AT THE SPAWN INSTEAD WOULD
// BE A TOMBSTONE.** A service has no promise, so nobody else will ever call `__gt_owner_done` for it — the
// thread is its own consumer. But `emitGtIsDropped` reads exactly that ticket to mean *"the promise is gone,
// do not RUN this thread"*, so a ticket added at spawn would make a never-yet-run service read as abandoned
// to every popper (`GtRuntime.emitGtIsDropped`). Added here it is the honest statement it looks like: this
// thread is finished, and the strand runner that switched into it supplies the runner's half.
//
// ⭐⭐ **THE GREEN THREAD IS READ HERE AND IS NOT A PARAMETER, BECAUSE THE MAXON-TIER LOOP HAS NO WAY TO NAME
// ONE.** `<T>.__loop` is ordinary program code (`ServiceLoop`) — its two parameters are the state and the
// mailbox, and there is no expression in the language that means "the green thread I am running on". Taking
// it as a parameter therefore left the loop passing ONE argument to a two-parameter entry, and `rdx` carried
// whatever the preceding `__mm_decref` left in it straight into `__gt_owner_done`. **MEASURED: a service
// whose state has TWO fields segfaulted where the same program with one field ran clean** — the difference
// being only which garbage the state's drop happened to leave behind.
//
// ⚠ `emitLoadCurrentGt`'s precondition — the scheduler is initialized — is satisfied by construction and not
// by convention: this function's only caller is a body RUNNING on a green thread the scheduler created.
function buildMboxServiceExit(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxServiceExitName, returnType: StdReturnType.void, paramCount: 1, paramTypes: oneI64Param())
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(1)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var freeMbox = module.addBlock(func, label: b"exitfree", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var doneBlock = module.addBlock(func, label: b"exitdone", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var answerShutdown = module.addBlock(func, label: b"exitanswershutdown", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var ownerDone = module.addBlock(func, label: b"exitownerdone", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 1)
	let mbox = 0
	let selfGt = emitLoadCurrentGt(module, block: entry, ids: ids)

	// ⭐⭐ **THE PILL'S REPLY IS READ BEFORE THE MAILBOX CAN BE FREED, AND ANSWERED AFTER.** The load has
	// to precede the release below — this thread may be the mailbox's last owner — while the completion has
	// to follow the state drop the loop performed one call earlier, which is the whole point of parking the
	// cell on the mailbox rather than completing it in the pill's arm.
	let shutdownReply = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffShutdownReply, ids: ids)
	let priorRefs = emitMboxCountStep(module, block: entry, mbox: mbox, offset: MboxOffRefs, delta: MboxCountDown, ids: ids)
	let wasLastRef = emitMboxWasLastOwner(module, block: entry, prior: priorRefs, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.condBranch(wasLastRef, thenBlockId: freeMbox.id, elseBlockId: doneBlock.id))

	emitMboxFree(module, block: freeMbox, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	module.setTerminator(freeMbox, op: StdOp.branch(doneBlock.id))

	// A service stopped by its LAST HANDLE DROP never received a pill, so the slot is the slab's zero and
	// there is nothing to answer.
	let noReply = emitConst(module, block: doneBlock, value: 0, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: doneBlock, value: shutdownReply, pred: StdCmpPred.ne, against: 0, whenTrue: answerShutdown, whenFalse: ownerDone, ids: ids)

	module.appendOp(answerShutdown, op: StdOp.call(ids.mint(), callee: GtCellCompleteName, args: threeArgs(shutdownReply, second: noReply, third: noReply)))
	module.setTerminator(answerShutdown, op: StdOp.branch(ownerDone.id))

	module.appendOp(ownerDone, op: StdOp.call(ids.mint(), callee: GtOwnerDoneName, args: argsOf(selfGt)))
	module.setTerminator(ownerDone, op: StdOp.retVoid)

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxServiceExit'

// `__mbox_abandon(mbox, box)`. See `MboxAbandonName`.
function buildMboxAbandon(module StdModule)
	var func = IrFunction.createFromStd(MboxAbandonName, returnType: StdReturnType.void, paramCount: 2, paramTypes: twoI64Params(), needsGreenThreadStackGuard: true, pinsItsThread: true)
	var ids = ValueMinter.create(2)

	var entry = module.addBlock(func, label: b"entry", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	emitParams(module, block: entry, count: 2)
	let mbox = 0
	let box = 1

	let abandonFn = emitLoadField(module, block: entry, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffAbandonFn, ids: ids)
	module.appendOp(entry, op: StdOp.callIndirect(ids.mint(), calleeReg: abandonFn, resultType: StdReturnType.void, argFloatMask: 0, args: argsOf(box)))
	module.setTerminator(entry, op: StdOp.retVoid)

	module.functions.push(func)
end 'buildMboxAbandon'

// ⭐⭐ **WHAT `__gt_register_park`'s MAILBOX ARM DOES — emitted HERE because the mailbox's fields are this
// file's, and the arm is one act over them.** The caller holds `__sched_lock` and has
// just handed this function a green thread that WANTS to park on `arg`. Two answers, and the RE-CHECK is
// what makes the first one possible at all:
//
//   • **A REQUEST ARRIVED, OR THE MAILBOX CLOSED, SINCE THE RECEIVE RELEASED THE LOCK.** The park is
//     UNDONE: nothing will ever wake this thread, because the event it was waiting for has already happened
//     and its waker found `parkedGt` still 0. The thread is readied, since it has already switched away and
//     is on no queue.
//   • **NEITHER.** The thread registers itself as the mailbox's `parkedGt` and goes `waiting`, which is what
//     the next `__mbox_send` or `__mbox_close` will find.
//
// ⚠⚠ **THE RE-CHECK IS CORRECT, AND A FIRE-AND-FORGET SERVICE CANNOT SHOW IT MISSING.** With it
// disabled (both comparisons forced true, so the park is always registered)
// `multicore-stress/service-torture` neither hangs nor leaks, because there are TWO WAKE SOURCES
// and the second is UNCONDITIONAL: a lost wake strands a message only until the NEXT event on that
// mailbox, and the last handle's drop calls `__mbox_close`, which takes the mailbox lock and wakes
// whoever is parked. So a missed send costs LATENCY, and the close repairs it before the process
// can exit.
//
// ⛔ **THAT IS AN ARGUMENT ABOUT OBSERVABILITY, NOT ABOUT THE WINDOW, AND THE WINDOW IS REAL.** An awaiter
// parked on a reply cell has no `__mbox_close` to rescue it, and there the lost wake is a hang with
// no second source. The re-check costs two loads under the mailbox lock.
//
// It terminates `cur` into `cont`, handing it the wake debt as `cont`'s one block argument:
// `__gt_strand_next` owns the release and pays the debt after it, as it does for every arm of
// `__gt_register_park`.
export function emitMboxRegisterPark(module StdModule, func IrFunction, cur IrBlock, gt ValueId, mbox ValueId, cont IrBlock, ids ValueMinter)
	var recheckClosed = module.addBlock(func, label: b"parkmboxclosed", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var undoPark = module.addBlock(func, label: b"parkmboxundo", heat: BlockHeat.normal)
	var registerWaiter = module.addBlock(func, label: b"parkmboxwait", heat: BlockHeat.normal)

	emitMboxLockEnter(module, block: cur, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	let head = emitLoadField(module, block: cur, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffHead, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: cur, value: head, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: 0, whenTrue: recheckClosed, whenFalse: undoPark, ids: ids)

	let closed = emitLoadField(module, block: recheckClosed, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffClosed, ids: ids)
	emitBranchOnCompare(module, block: recheckClosed, value: closed, pred: StdCmpPred.eq, against: 0, whenTrue: registerWaiter, whenFalse: undoPark, ids: ids)

	let waitingStatus = emitConst(module, block: registerWaiter, value: GtStatus.waiting.rawValue, ids: ids)
	emitStoreField(module, block: registerWaiter, record: mbox, offset: MboxOffParkedGt, value: gt)
	emitStoreField(module, block: registerWaiter, record: gt, offset: GtOffStatus, value: waitingStatus)
	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: registerWaiter, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	emitBranchWithDebt(module, from: registerWaiter, to: cont, debt: emitConst(module, block: registerWaiter, value: WakeDebtNone, ids: ids))

	emitMboxLockLeave(module, block: undoPark, mbox: mbox, ids: ids)
	emitBranchWithDebt(module, from: undoPark, to: cont, debt: emitGtReadyLocked(module, block: undoPark, gt: gt, ids: ids))
end 'emitMboxRegisterPark'
